  "body": "Found while fixing #1532.\n\nWhat happens: with the new Between setups option (default Pause), the program writes an M0 (or M1) after each setup's last operation. Fanuc and Tormach PathPilot also lift Z clear first and write a comment naming the next setup, read from the new `PARAM SetupChange \"<setup>\"` record. The other dialects that declare `afterModes` (Haas, Mazak, Doosan DNM, Sinumerik, Heidenhain, grblHAL, TinyG, the lathe and wire posts) ignore that record: they write the stop where they write an operator's own stop, with no Z lift and no comment, so the operator gets a bare stop with the tool at clearance height and no word on what to do.\n\nExpected: each afterModes dialect reads `SetupChange` and, at a setup-change stop, lifts Z by its own retract (the one it uses before a tool change) and writes a comment (or its message form) naming the next setup, as `assets/posts/fanuc.cps` and `assets/posts/tormach.cps` do.\n\nEvidence: `crates/app/tests/between_setups.rs` pins Fanuc and Tormach only; `crates/app/src/posting_setup_change.rs` writes the record for every post.\n\nDone means: every built-in afterModes mill dialect writes the Z lift and the next-setup comment before a setup-change stop, each pinned by a post test; lathe and wire dialects either do the same or are named in the issue as not applicable.\n",
